From: Michael Tretter <m.tretter@pengutronix.de>
Date: Wed, 28 Jan 2026 22:25:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tee: optee: add system_data driver

system_data is a OP-TEE TA that allows to store variables. Different
types of variables are supported:

- unrestricted
- write-once
- rollback-protected

write-once variables are allowed to be written exactly once.
rollback-protected variables have a (usually 8 byte) counter at the
start of the variable. Updates are only allowed when this counter is
increased with the write. Unrestricted variables do not have any
restrictions.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Michael Tretter <m.tretter@pengutronix.de>
Signed-off-by: Sascha Hauer <s.hauer@pengutronix.de>
---
 drivers/tee/optee/Kconfig          |   7 +
 drivers/tee/optee/Makefile         |   1 +
 drivers/tee/optee/system_data.c    | 273 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/tee/optee/system_data_ta.h |  41 ++++++
 include/system_data.h              |  32 +++++
 5 files changed, 354 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/tee/optee/system_data.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/tee/optee/system_data_ta.h
 create mode 100644 include/system_data.h

diff --git a/drivers/tee/optee/Kconfig b/drivers/tee/optee/Kconfig
index 73e77d0559c4..ad200b3a9e2a 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/optee/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/tee/optee/Kconfig
@@ -47,6 +47,13 @@ config OPTEE_RKSECURE
 	  Enable this option to use the Rockchip Secure Boot PTA to read or
 	  write the secure boot OTP fuses of an rk3588 SoC.
 
+config OPTEE_SYSTEM_DATA
+	bool "Secure Data TA support"
+	depends on OPTEE
+	help
+	  Enable this option to use the System Data TA to store and read
+	  rollback protected data from the secure storage.
+
 endif
 
 config OF_FIXUP_OPTEE
